{"_id":"c301000000000001","flags":{"runyth-compendium":{"contentHash":"d65faa3a3addafb35112b006f3a0fcc34cd31debf36c4a3ac5a2f9af6e08c8fa","contentLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","contentVersion":"1.0.0","entryId":"how-to-use","kind":"journal","managed":true,"provenance":"Runyth","schemaVersion":1,"summary":"What the Compendium ships, how it stays system-agnostic, and where the licence lives."}},"folder":null,"name":"How to Use Runyth Compendium","ownership":{"default":0},"pages":[{"_id":"pg01010000000000","flags":{},"name":"The Compendium in any world","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":100,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>The Compendium in any world</h1><p>Runyth Compendium is a content library for Foundry Virtual Tabletop. Its packs are system-agnostic: they install and open in any world, whatever the game system underneath offers. Armory and Features carry Item documents without system-specific data; importing one gives your world's system a clean document to fill. World Elements are journal text; Tables are roll tables.</p><p>System-agnostic means deliberate: records carry no system block at all. A companion module, such as a D&D 5e 2024 companion, gives selected records real system fields with its own tested release.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"},{"_id":"pg01020000000000","flags":{},"name":"Licence per record","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":200,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Licence per record</h1><p>Every record in the Compendium is original Runyth homebrew content and is released under CC BY-SA 4.0. The licence is stamped on each record under the module's flags (contentLicence), and the text files in packs/_source carry the same statement. The module's source code around the content is AGPL-3.0-or-later; see LICENSE.</p><p>When you excerpt or adapt a record for your campaigns, share alike and attribute Runyth as the content's source.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"},{"_id":"pg01030000000000","flags":{},"name":"Growing the Compendium","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":300,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Growing the Compendium</h1><p>Records are authored as JSON under packs/_source and compiled by the repository tooling into deterministic NeDB packs, with a content hash stamped on each record. New records follow the naming and ID rules in this chapter's siblings, and every release of the Compendium publishes the whole set together.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"}],"sort":100}
{"_id":"c302000000000001","flags":{"runyth-compendium":{"contentHash":"a6948ef373a595d7143546bcbc0e24b305052066013ebad733fa8815c5d60f3f","contentLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","contentVersion":"1.0.0","entryId":"saltmarket-exchange","kind":"journal","managed":true,"provenance":"Runyth","schemaVersion":1,"summary":"A cosmopolitan trade hub where honest prices are enforced by brass and cordiality."}},"folder":null,"name":"The Saltmarket Exchange","ownership":{"default":0},"pages":[{"_id":"pg02010000000000","flags":{},"name":"The Exchange floor","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":100,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>The Saltmarket Exchange</h1><p>The Exchange is a covered market of the kind any port, crossroads or planar bazaar can host: a floor of leased stalls, a wall of posted tariffs, and an office of weights. Nothing on the floor is genuinely new; everything is honestly described or conspicuously not.</p><p>Its law is short. Weigh with the house scale when challenged. Shout the price before the bargain, not after. A buyer who lies about what they bring to the table loses the table.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"},{"_id":"pg02020000000000","flags":{},"name":"Brokers and wares","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":200,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Brokers and wares</h1><p>Brokers rent their stall under the salt arch, where the roof sweats in winter and drips in summer. The most reliable brokers keep their own scales, and the scale that tips for a living is a broker's proudest keepsake.</p><p>The common wares: charters of passage, honest maps of dishonest places, cellar inventories of three dead merchants, and jars whose contents are exactly as labelled. The rare wares are the ones the Exchange refuses to describe and sells only by reputation.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"},{"_id":"pg02030000000000","flags":{},"name":"Using the Exchange in your world","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":300,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Using the Exchange in your world</h1><p>Drop the Exchange wherever trade needs a dirty floor and clean brass. The associated roll table, Saltmarket Curiosities, supplies one notable stall or rumour. The Saltmarket Scale in the Armory pack is the house scale of a broker who paid well for it.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"}],"sort":200}
{"_id":"c303000000000001","flags":{"runyth-compendium":{"contentHash":"633eb0a32a817ab7e89309c170ff63e28b38951beed4fe7a086539ab370e0e11","contentLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","contentVersion":"1.0.0","entryId":"porchlight-compact","kind":"journal","managed":true,"provenance":"Runyth","schemaVersion":1,"summary":"A travellers' guild of shelter-keepers, lantern-tenders, and people who leave a light on."}},"folder":null,"name":"The Porchlight Compact","ownership":{"default":0},"pages":[{"_id":"pg03010000000000","flags":{},"name":"The Compact","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":100,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>The Porchlight Compact</h1><p>The Compact is an arrangement older than most roads: keepers of wayhouses, monasteries, canal locks and lighthouses agree to light a lamp for arriving strangers and to pass travellers onward with a note of introduction. It has no masters, no dues, and no uniforms; it keeps a roster, a lantern token, and a stubborn etiquette.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"},{"_id":"pg03020000000000","flags":{},"name":"Tokens and obligations","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":200,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Tokens and obligations</h1><p>A member carries a lantern token, a cheap stamped brass charm. Showing a token to another keeper asks for shelter first and questions later. In return the member owes three duties: take the watch when offered, leave the shelter as you found it, and tell the truth about the road behind you.</p><p>Breaking an obligation does not expel a member; it flips the token, and a flipped token can only be righted by hosting the person you wronged.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"},{"_id":"pg03030000000000","flags":{},"name":"Using the Compact in your world","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":300,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Using the Compact in your world</h1><p>Place hostelries and keepers along any route your players travel. The Porchlight Lantern in the Armory pack is a first-choice heirloom of Compact keepers; Hearthprayer in the Features pack is the small ritual a keeper teaches a promising guest.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"}],"sort":300}
{"_id":"c304000000000001","flags":{"runyth-compendium":{"contentHash":"e4306c9bc9ea0b570bbbb4af22f3b564b984a40115b0022a20fde5b852efc0a2","contentLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","contentVersion":"1.0.0","entryId":"licence-and-credits","kind":"journal","managed":true,"provenance":"Runyth","schemaVersion":1,"summary":"The source and content licence pair of the Compendium, and the credits behind it."}},"folder":null,"name":"Licence & Credits","ownership":{"default":0},"pages":[{"_id":"pg04010000000000","flags":{},"name":"Licences","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":100,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Licences</h1><p>The module's source code is licensed AGPL-3.0-or-later. The content records it ships (items, features, world elements, tables) are licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, and every record stamps its own licence in the module's flags.</p><p>Source code licence: AGPL-3.0-or-later. Content licence: CC BY-SA 4.0. The two licence fields are exclusive by policy: source stays AGPL, content stays CC BY-SA.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"},{"_id":"pg04020000000000","flags":{},"name":"Credits","ownership":{"default":-1},"sort":200,"system":{},"text":{"content":"<h1>Credits</h1><p>Runyth Compendium is a Runyth project, authored for the Runyth fleet and for any Foundry world that wants company. Attribution for content reuse: Runyth, with a link to the module repository, shared under the same licence.</p>","format":1},"title":{"level":1,"show":false},"type":"text"}],"sort":400}
